`bmb check` does not report the diagnostic E0433 yet: a value is used whole after one of its fields was moved. It came with the commit "2O-03: owned fields and partial moves". Implement it. Examples of what `bmb check` must print (one JSON line per diagnostic; the path in `file` is the one given on the command line), each after the source line it points at:

    whole(c)
    {"code": "E0433", "severity": "error", "message": "`c` is used after its field `c.a.data` was moved", "file": "err/owned_fields.bmb", "line": 19, "col": 15, "end_line": 19, "end_col": 16, "fix": {"message": "assign `c.a.data` again before this use, or use the other fields"}}

    let u: Slot = t;
    {"code": "E0433", "severity": "error", "message": "`t` is used after its field `t.v` was moved", "file": "err/owned_fields.bmb", "line": 66, "col": 23, "end_line": 66, "end_col": 24, "fix": {"message": "assign `t.v` again before this use, or use the other fields"}}

Everything else the program prints must stay as it is.

